   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "Each term has the form \\( \\frac{x^{n}}{n!} \\) with \\( x = -5 \\), so this is the Maclaurin series for \\( e^{x} \\) evaluated at \\( x = -5 \\).",
         "mathjson": -5
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "That series converges for every \\( x \\), and its full sum from \\( n = 0 \\) is \\( e^{-5} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Exp",
            -5
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "The series starts at \\( n = 0 \\), so nothing is removed and the series equals \\( e^{-5} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Exp",
            -5
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 4,
         "text": "The value of the series is \\( e^{-5} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
